<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Townsend</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815–1886</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Townsend was an English missionary of the Church Missionary Society who worked among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> from the 1840s. He settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeokuta">Abeokuta</a> in 1846, founded churches and schools, and in 1859 started Iwe Irohin, one of the first newspapers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, printed in Yoruba. He became an influential adviser to Egba leaders and remained in Yoruba country until 1876.</p></div>
